          "text": "Non-profit PurposesAsset Protection",
          "ph_type": "title",
          "ph_idx": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "sp",
          "id": 3,
          "name": "Content Placeholder 2",
          "x": 493094,
          "y": 1485899,
          "cx": 11332560,
          "cy": 4298315,
          "prst": null,
          "flipH": null,
          "flipV": null,
          "text": "Asset protection is critical to fundraising in parishes/dioceses where future friendliness toward classical education and great art is in questionBarbarian bishops and modernist priests have destroyed much church art and sold off numerous assets to pay abuse settlementsMost people have stories of friends/family saving church art from literal dumpstersNon-profit can hold assets in trust and give them away to other schools if unfriendly powers take control and want to dispose of the art",
          "ph_type": "body",
          "ph_idx": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "slide6.xml",
      "shapes": [
        {
          "type": "sp",
          "id": 2,
          "name": "Title 1",
          "x": 493095,
          "y": 1227,
          "cx": 10515600,
          "cy": 1141774,
          "prst": null,
          "flipH": null,
          "flipV": null,
          "text": "Non-profit PurposesProject and Concept Promotion",
          "ph_type": "title",
          "ph_idx": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "sp",
          "id": 3,
          "name": "Content Placeholder 2",
          "x": 493094,
          "y": 1485899,
          "cx": 11332560,
          "cy": 4298315,
          "prst": null,
          "flipH": null,
          "flipV": null,
          "text": "Holy Child is pioneering something newNever before have modern printing methods been combined with the ever-growing library of high resolution photos of museum paintings to bring the best masterpiece paintings in the western canon to schoolsThe classical school movement is rapidly expanding and pioneering new ways to bring the a traditional education to the modern worldMany schools would likely be interested if they could see this projectWays to promote conceptSpeak at educational conferencesNews coveragePublishing in academic journals and educational magazinesPartnerships with local art museumsPartnerships with other schools",
          "ph_type": "body",
          "ph_idx": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "file": "slide7.xml",
      "shapes": [
        {
          "type": "sp",
          "id": 2,
          "name": "Title 1",
          "x": 493095,
          "y": 1227,
          "cx": 10515600,
          "cy": 1141774,
          "prst": null,
          "flipH": null,
          "flipV": null,
          "text": "Non-profit PurposesConnecting School Communities and Museums",
          "ph_type": "title",
          "ph_idx": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "sp",
          "id": 3,
          "name": "Content Placeholder 2",
          "x": 493094,
          "y": 1143001,
          "cx": 11332560,
          "cy": 4641213,
          "prst": null,
          "flipH": null,
          "flipV": null,
          "text": "Reproductions shouldn\u2019t be the only art children seeMost masterpiece paintings live in museumsTraveling exhibits bring masterpieces to even smaller cities like AlbuquerqueReserving a section of wall to display the best of local art museums would encourage families to visitRequires working with museum staff to acquire rights and select pieces for displayProvides visibility of museum exhibits to school familiesProvides visibility of school in the wider communityWin-win for families, museum, and schoolStrong partnerships generate opportunity for positive media interest and coverageMuseum staff will likely lead this effort",
          "ph_type": "body",
          "ph_idx": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
